{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788286365,"nonce":"NZR6V9IumQ0PiSEhgeHVMAam6Q8=","message":"M2 IS MET — a room colonists built from `templates/bedroom.ir.json`, on a bench,\nwith the game's own `Room` analysis calling it a bedroom. Session 18. Full record\nand evidence: `accept/runs/s18-20260901/`.\n\nBench `_RimWorld-Agent`, sid `20260901T180111`, `--quicktest` 250x250 temperate\nforest, assembly at `6b4422c` (no `*.cs` changed since that `Build:`). Watched at\n2560x1600 throughout.\n\n## The run\n\n`find-rect --w 5 --h 7 --near 121,129 --require buildable --require unroofed\n--require reachable-from:111,127` -\u003e `at [119,126]`, then\n\n    rwa place-layout templates/bedroom.ir.json --origin 119,126 --stuff '*=WoodLog'\n\n    preflight  ok true, checked 22, failed 0\n    placed_count 22, layout_id \"ly-1\", rolled_back false, journal_seq 38\n\nTwo `advance` calls later (2000 then 6000 ticks — see the `fc287ba` comment for\nwhy that number was a guess and should not have to be), 22 journal `construction`\nrows, every one `kind: \"completed\"`, every one `worker: \"Danielle\"`, spanning\nticks 1264-4444. `construction`: `blueprints 0, frames 0`.\n\n`room --id 66`:\n\n    role \"Bedroom\"        role_label \"bedroom\"\n    proper true           indoors true          regions 1\n    cells 15              touches_map_edge false\n    open_roof_cells 0     uses_outdoor_temp false     temp_c 22.7 (outdoor 4)\n    contains  Wall x19, all WoodLog, all roofed\n    beds  [{id 37916, at [121,131], owners: [Izzy]}]\n\nIzzy claimed the bed by sleeping in it under advance — `JobDriver_LayDown` -\u003e\n`Toils_Bed.ClaimBedIfNonMedical`, no verb involved.\n\nJournal seq 12-62: 22 `construction`, 19 `dev`, 5 `alert_on`, 3 `action`, 2\n`alert_off`. **No `warning` and no `error` rows** — zero red errors.\n\n## Against this issue's own Acceptance, honestly\n\nThe M2 rehearsal bullet asks for \"parametric 5x7 bedroom placed as blueprints on\na fresh map at a find-rect-chosen origin; pawns complete it under advance; Room\nrole=Bedroom, enclosed, **heated by placed heater**; zero red errors.\" Everything\nbut the heater is met as written. `templates/bedroom.ir.json` contains no heater —\nits elements are Wall, Bed, TorchLamp, Door — so that clause cannot be satisfied\nby this template and was not attempted. The room holds 22.7 C against 4 C\noutdoors on enclosure alone. Either the template gains a heater or the bullet\nloses it; flagging rather than deciding, since it is this spec's own text.\n\nThe other two Acceptance bullets are UNTOUCHED by this run and remain open:\ninstant mode was never called, and no deliberately-colliding layout was placed.\nThis run says nothing about either.\n\n## Three defects, filed\n\n- `54b0c9a` — `shortfall[]` said `short_by: 185` while 869 reachable unforbidden\n  WoodLog sat ten cells from the site, because `in_stockpiles` is\n  `map.resourceCounter` and a quicktest map has no stockpile zone. The room was\n  then built out of that \"missing\" wood. `MaterialBill`'s own header already\n  documents the cause; the defect is that `short_by` draws a conclusion from a\n  number the comment says cannot support one. `construction`'s `missing[]` too.\n- `36999fd` — `construction` has no `layout_id` scope, and silently ignored the\n  arg while answering whole-map and reporting success. `place-layout` mints an\n  `ly-N` and `cancel-layout` takes one; the progress verb cannot be asked.\n- Comment on `fc287ba` — no state predicate, so \"advance until the room is done\"\n  was two guessed tick counts.\n\n## One correction to the M2 brief's stated premise, from the decompiled source\n\nThe brief (and the working assumption going in) was that `role: \"Bedroom\"`\nrequires a bed OWNER and that an unowned bed scores Barracks. **Not true in 1.6\nfor a one-bed room.** `RimWorld/RoomRoleWorker_Bedroom.IsBedroomHelper` counts an\nowner-less bed into `num` when `bed.def.building.bed_emptyCountsForBarracks`\n(default `true`, `RimWorld/BuildingProperties.cs:196`) and opens its verdict with\n`if (num == 1 \u0026\u0026 num2 == 0) { return true; }`. `RoomRoleWorker_Barracks.GetScore`\nreturns `0f` whenever `RoomRoleWorker_Bedroom.IsBedroom` is true, so Barracks\ncannot win it. The brief's rule holds from two empty beds up.\n\nRecorded as a SOURCE READING, not a measurement: Izzy claimed the bed during this\nrun, so the one-bed-unowned case was never observed live. It matters for whoever\nwrites the acceptance suite, which would otherwise advance until a colonist\nsleeps in order to reach a state that was already reached.","files":null}]}